---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import publication from '../data/publication.json';
import release from '../data/release.json';
import { isReleaseReady } from '../lib/release.mjs';
const ready = isReleaseReady(release);
---

<Layout
  title="Download & setup — Peak"
  description="Install Peak free from Microsoft Store. Windows requirements, Codex and Claude connection setup, Store updates, and support."
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <span class="eyebrow">
        <span class="tiny-cross">+</span> PEAK FOR WINDOWS
      </span>
      <h1>
        A small addition.
        <br />A clearer <span class="heading-emphasis">desktop.</span>
      </h1>
      <p>
        Free for personal and workplace use, on unlimited devices. Your
        compatible provider tools and subscriptions supply the live readings.
      </p>
    </header>
    <div class="page-grid">
      <div>
        <section class="content-block" aria-labelledby="downloads-title">
          <h2 id="downloads-title">Get Peak from Microsoft Store</h2>
          <div class="release-facts">
            <span>
              Requirements<strong>{release.requirements}</strong>
            </span>
            <span>
              Publisher<strong>{publication.publisherName}</strong>
            </span>
            <span>
              Price<strong>Free · personal &amp; workplace use</strong>
            </span>
          </div>
          <article class="download-card store-download-card">
            <Icon name="window" size={28} />
            <h3>One place to install and update.</h3>
            <p>
              Open Peak’s official listing, select Download or View in Store,
              and follow Microsoft Store’s installation steps. Launch Peak from
              your Start menu.
            </p>
            {ready ? (
              <a class="button button-primary" href={release.storeUrl}>
                Get it on Microsoft Store <Icon name="diagonal" size={18} />
              </a>
            ) : (
              <p>
                The Store listing is temporarily unavailable. Please check back
                or contact support.
              </p>
            )}
            <p>
              Microsoft Store manages installation and package updates. The .NET
              runtime is included. Live usage requires the provider setup below.
            </p>
          </article>
        </section>
        <section id="setup" class="content-block">
          <h2>Start with the providers you use</h2>
          <p>
            New installations start with providers disabled. Open Settings →
            Providers, read the access explanation, and enable the integrations
            you want. Peak does not supply an AI account, subscription, or
            credits.
          </p>
          <h3>Codex usage</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              Turn on <strong>Codex usage</strong> in Peak’s Settings →
              Providers.
            </li>
            <li>
              Peak checks for the Windows CLI and reuses your existing ChatGPT
              login.
            </li>
            <li>
              If needed, choose <strong>Install &amp; connect</strong>, then{' '}
              <strong>Sign in &amp; connect</strong>. Complete the provider’s
              sign-in screen.
            </li>
            <li>Save changes. Peak refreshes your usage automatically.</li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Peak respects Codex’s existing login configuration and reads its
            local app-server interface. Provider credentials stay with Codex.
            API-key billing is separate from ChatGPT subscription limits.
            <a href="https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/codex/cli">
              Official Codex setup
            </a>
            .
          </p>
          <h3>Codex task activity</h3>
          <p>
            Choose <strong>Connect task activity</strong> in Peak. It adds its
            observer entries while preserving unrelated hooks. Use{' '}
            <code>/hooks</code> in Codex to review and trust them, then
            reconnect existing chats. Hook support, your explicit trust, and a
            local supported environment are required for observer-based review
            reporting.
          </p>
          <p>
            Bounded local logs may also provide activity and question
            observations. Missing approval observations do not mean there are no
            approvals. Reported states can become stale; respond in Codex.
          </p>
          <h3>Claude usage</h3>
          <ol>
            <li>
              Turn on <strong>Claude usage</strong>. Peak installs its usage
              bridge automatically.
            </li>
            <li>
              Choose <strong>Install &amp; connect</strong> if Claude Code is
              missing, then <strong>Open Claude Code</strong>.
            </li>
            <li>
              Sign in with Claude Pro or Max. Send a prompt and wait for its
              first response. Restart existing Claude Code sessions to load the
              bridge.
            </li>
            <li>
              Save changes. Peak receives usage as Claude Code reports it.
            </li>
          </ol>
          <p>
            Use the Windows Claude Code CLI. The Claude chat website or desktop
            app alone, and API-key accounts, do not supply these personal
            subscription readings to Peak. Peak preserves an existing
            status-line command’s output and a protected restoration backup.
            <a href="https://code.claude.com/docs/en/setup">
              Official Claude Code setup
            </a>
            .
          </p>
          <p>
            Installing and signing in take effect immediately; canceling Peak’s
            other preferences does not undo them. Readings can become stale
            between CLI activity. Reconnect after changing accounts. Claude task
            or approval monitoring is not included.
          </p>
          <h3>If a command is not recognized</h3>
          <p>
            Reopen PowerShell after installing, then check{' '}
            <code>codex --version</code> or <code>claude --version</code>.
            Restart Peak if it was open during installation. Use connection
            setup above to install a missing CLI. If Claude stays waiting,
            receive a response in a new Claude Code session and check that a
            project-level status line is not replacing Peak’s user-level bridge.
          </p>
        </section>
        <section id="updates" class="content-block">
          <h2>Update, disconnect, or uninstall</h2>
          <p>
            Microsoft Store delivers updates according to your Store settings.
            To check manually, open the Store’s Library and check for updates.
            Peak has no separate updater.
          </p>
          <p>
            Provider disconnection removes only Peak-owned integration entries.
            Claude restoration is applied only when the installed status line
            still matches; unrelated settings are preserved. Restart existing
            CLI sessions to unload integrations already loaded there.
          </p>
          <p>
            Before uninstalling, disconnect integrations in Peak’s Privacy
            settings and restart existing provider CLI sessions. Then remove
            Peak in Windows Settings → Apps → Installed apps.
          </p>
          <p>
            The Store edition keeps copied bridges and protected restoration
            information in your per-user data folder, outside the installed
            package. Use Peak’s Privacy controls for local-data cleanup; retain
            restoration backups until provider settings are safely restored.
            Original provider logs remain separate.
          </p>
        </section>
      </div>
      <aside class="page-aside">
        <div class="aside-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">GOOD TO KNOW</span>
          <h2>
            Free to use.
            <br />
            Yours to set up.
          </h2>
          <p>
            No Peak payment, activation, account, device cap, or expiry in the
            freeware release.
          </p>
          <p>
            Source ownership is retained. Freeware does not mean open source.
          </p>
          <div class="aside-links">
            <a href="/terms/">Read the freeware terms ↗</a>
            <a href="/privacy/">Read the privacy notice ↗</a>
            <a href="/notices/">Third-party notices ↗</a>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="aside-card">
          <span class="eyebrow">NEED A HAND?</span>
          <h2>Setup & support</h2>
          <p>
            {publication.supportEmail
              ? 'Send a sanitized report to the dedicated support mailbox.'
              : 'The dedicated support mailbox will be published before launch. The support page explains what to include in a report.'}
          </p>
          <a class="button" href="/support/">
            Support guide <Icon name="arrow" size={15} />
          </a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
